                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00N/81: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-12T15:00:00-06:00">July 12, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. Referring to my despatch No. 2298, June 24 and others on the subject of
                    basing gunboat at Puntarenas. Commander of destroyer now at that port recommends
                    he be permitted to remain there until relieved by other vessel. I respectfully
                    recommend that this be done.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hornibrook</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
